    \item The Wannier approximation lies above all exact
          enumeration curves.
          This is a systematic effect of the $N/2$ constraint:
          the constraint suppresses disorder, keeping
          $\avgE{\COH}$ below the unconstrained Wannier value.
\end{itemize}

